## 5. Automated Scheduling Engine (Supabase `pg_cron`)

To initiate asynchronous batch runs directly from the Postgres data tier based on each user's designated `delivery_hour_utc`, we install a scheduled trigger calling the Next.js/Inngest endpoint via `pg_net`.

```sql
-- Enable HTTP networking extension inside Postgres
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "pg_net";

-- Create scheduling stored procedure for batch dispatch
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.trigger_daily_video_generation_job()
RETURNS void
LANGUAGE plpgsql
SECURITY DEFINER
AS $$
DECLARE
  v_request_id BIGINT;
BEGIN
  -- Dispatches webhook trigger to Next.js API route
  SELECT net.http_post(
    url := 'https://microlearn-pro.vercel.app/api/inngest',
    headers := jsonb_build_object(
      'Content-Type', 'application/json',
      'Authorization', 'Bearer ' || current_setting('app.settings.service_role_key', true)
    ),
    body := jsonb_build_object(
      'name', 'pipeline/video.batch.trigger',
      'data', jsonb_build_object('scheduledDate', CURRENT_DATE::text)
    )
  ) INTO v_request_id;
END;
$$;

-- Schedule Cron Job: Runs at the top of every hour (UTC) to process staggered timezones
SELECT cron.schedule(
  'process-hourly-video-deliveries',
  '0 * * * *',
  $$ SELECT public.trigger_daily_video_generation_job(); $$
);
```

