## 3. Prefetching Strategy

Smooth vertical feed switching requires near-zero buffer starvation. When an active video reaches index $N$, downloading must anticipate index $N+1$ without choking the current stream's bandwidth.

### 3.1 Sliding Window State Machine
The architecture categorizes slides into 4 states:

```
[Index N-2] ----------> Dormant / Placeholder Only (DOM Recycled, Memory Purged)
[Index N-1] ----------> Paused (Retained in memory for instantaneous upward back-scroll)
[Index N]   ----------> ACTIVE (Unmuted/Playing, max bitrate allocation)
[Index N+1] ----------> PREFETCHING (Preloads first 2 HLS segments via Range Request / link tag)
[Index N+2] ----------> Warm-up (Head request for HLS playlist / poster image fetch)
```

### 3.2 Network-Aware Adaptive Prefetch Hook (`lib/hooks/use-feed-prefetch.ts`)
This hook monitors browser connection metrics (`navigator.connection`) and manages speculative chunk fetching.

```typescript
'use client';

import { useEffect } from 'react';
import type { DeliveryWithVideo } from '@/lib/types/feed';

interface NetworkInformation extends EventTarget {
  effectiveType: 'slow-2g' | '2g' | '3g' | '4g';
  saveData: boolean;
  downlink: number;
}

export function useFeedPrefetch(
  deliveries: DeliveryWithVideo[],
  activeIndex: number
) {
  useEffect(() => {
    // Check for Data Saver or slow connections
    const nav = navigator as unknown as { connection?: NetworkInformation };
    const connection = nav.connection;
    const isSaveData = connection?.saveData;
    const isSlowNetwork = connection?.effectiveType === '2g' || connection?.effectiveType === 'slow-2g';

    if (isSaveData || isSlowNetwork) {
      // Restrict prefetching completely on metered or degraded connections
      return;
    }

    const nextDelivery = deliveries[activeIndex + 1];
    if (!nextDelivery) return;

    // 1. Speculatively prefetch poster image using standard Image object
    const posterImg = new window.Image();
    posterImg.src = nextDelivery.video.thumbnailUrl;

    // 2. Prefetch the first 4 seconds (init segment + first 2 media chunks)
    // In HLS, fetching the master manifest and sub-manifest primes the HTTP cache
    const manifestLink = document.createElement('link');
    manifestLink.rel = 'prefetch';
    manifestLink.as = 'fetch';
    manifestLink.href = nextDelivery.video.streamUrl;
    manifestLink.crossOrigin = 'anonymous';

    document.head.appendChild(manifestLink);

    return () => {
      if (document.head.contains(manifestLink)) {
        document.head.removeChild(manifestLink);
      }
    };
  }, [deliveries, activeIndex]);
}
```

### 3.3 Prefetch Execution Metrics Table

| Network Type | Prefetch Action | Buffer Cap ($N+1$) | Auto-Resolution Cap |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **4G / WiFi (>5Mbps)** | Full Manifest + Segments 0-2 (4s) | 6.0 Seconds | 1080p |
| **3G (1-3Mbps)** | Master Playlist Only + Poster | 2.0 Seconds (Segment 0) | 720p |
| **2G / SaveData** | Poster Image Only (No video preload) | 0 Seconds | 540p |

